{"id": "EUVD-2026-65225", "enisaUuid": "1960782c-72cf-31e9-8fdf-2aa294ef4ac2", "description": "GitPython before 3.1.59 contains an arbitrary file read vulnerability in TagReference.create() where a positional reference parameter bypasses the unsafe option guard. Attackers can supply a reference value like --file=<path> to read arbitrary files, with contents returned in the annotated tag message.", "datePublished": "2026-08-25T01:30:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-08T15:25:09", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/gitpython-developers/GitPython/security/advisories/GHSA-3wxw-xv34-2frg", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gitpython-before-arbitrary-file-read-via-tagreference-create"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3wxw-xv34-2frg", "GHSA-6rj2-96f5-chj9", "CVE-2026-78679", "PYSEC-2026-3837"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a1341729-60fd-385b-89df-68ec023a5163", "product": {"name": "GitPython", "vendor": {"name": "gitpython-developers"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.1.59"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2c272a7c-397c-31e4-a91d-0dd796648ca0", "vendor": {"name": "gitpython-developers"}}], "isExploited": false}